MAKE
====

Build tool - compile multiple files easily.


BASIC
-----
make

Reads Makefile and compiles.


WHAT IT DOES
------------
• Compiles only changed files
• Saves time on big projects
• Automates build process


MAKEFILE
--------
Create file named "Makefile":

all: program

program: main.c
	gcc main.c -o program

clean:
	rm program


COMMON TARGETS
---------------
make            Build program
make clean      Delete binaries
make rebuild    Clean then build
make run        Run program


EXAMPLE MAKEFILE
-----------------
CC = gcc
CFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra
TARGET = myprogram

all: $(TARGET)

$(TARGET): main.c helper.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) main.c helper.c -o $(TARGET)

clean:
	rm $(TARGET)

run: $(TARGET)
	./$(TARGET)


BENEFITS
--------
• One command to build
• Automatic compilation
• Skip unchanged files
• Share with others


TIPS
----
Indentation matters in Makefile.
Use Tab not spaces before commands.
Simple but powerful tool.
